WEBVTT


00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:05.460
Although our knitting machines can't
cross cables automatically, using

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.260
a ribber to create knit and purl
stitches of traditional cable knitting

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.570
makes the process a whole lot easier.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:19.010
For these mini cables, cast on and set
the needle arrangement to look like this.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.690
Now I prefer to cross my cables
on the main bed, but you could

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.260
reverse this needle arrangement
and cross the cables on the ribber

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:40.410
.
I also chose to knit six rows
between cables, but that's up to you.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.720
For a hand manipulated pattern,
this one goes pretty quickly and the

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.450
results are so worth the extra effort.

